+---
+id: dl-002-applypatch-works-on-a-deep-copy-and-returns-it-so-the-input-is-never-mutated
+type: decision-log
+title: "applyPatch works on a deep copy and returns it, so the input is never mutated"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+The services that use `applyPatch` need the input document to stay as it was: they keep it as a
+snapshot, compare it with the result, and retry with another patch. RFC 6902 describes the operations
+as changes to a document and does not say whether the input is changed.
+
+## Decision
+
+`applyPatch` makes one deep copy of the document, applies every operation to that copy in place, and
+returns the copy. The input is never written to, including when a later operation fails.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Each call copies the whole document, whatever the size of the patch.
+- A failed patch needs no rollback: the copy is discarded and the input is untouched.
+- Callers get a new value every time, even for an empty patch, so they can compare it with the input.
