@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+---
+id: dl-003-applypatch-is-all-or-nothing-any-invalid-operation-throws-and-no-result-is-returned
+type: decision-log
+title: "applyPatch is all-or-nothing: any invalid operation throws and no result is returned"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+A patch describes one change. A partly applied patch would produce a document that no caller asked
+for, and the caller would have no reliable way to tell how far it got.
+
+## Decision
+
+The whole patch is validated before any operation runs: it must be an array, and each operation must be
+an object with a known `op`, a string `path` that is a valid JSON Pointer, a `value` for add, replace
+and test, and a string `from` that is a valid pointer for move and copy. The operations then run in
+order, and the first one that fails throws. A failing `test` throws too, since RFC 6902 section 4.6
+makes it fail the patch. Removing the whole document throws, because no `JsonValue` represents an
+empty document.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- An invalid patch is rejected even when its problem is in an operation that would run last.
+- Every failure is an `Error`, and its message names the pointer involved.
+- The `value` is checked only for presence. The input is typed `JsonValue`, and callers pass parsed
+  JSON, so deep validation was not added.
