@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+---
+id: dl-004-patch-values-and-move-copy-sources-are-cloned-so-the-result-never-shares-structure-with-the-patch-or-input
+type: decision-log
+title: "Patch values and move/copy sources are cloned, so the result never shares structure with the patch or input"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+RFC 6902 says `add`, `replace` and `test` take a `value`, and `copy` and `move` take the value at
+`from`. If the result held the same arrays or objects as the patch, a later change to the result would
+change the patch, and the reverse. Shared structure with the input would also let a change to the result
+be seen through the input.
+
+## Decision
+
+Values inserted by `add` and `replace`, and values taken from `from` by `copy` and `move`, are deep-copied
+before they are inserted. Members are set with `Object.defineProperty`, so a name such as `__proto__`
+becomes an ordinary own member and never changes a prototype.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Inserting a large value costs a copy of that value.
+- The same patch can be applied to several documents without the results sharing data.
+- Callers can reuse or change a patch after applying it.
